# Form Development Patterns

## Form Libraries
- **React Hook Form**: Primary form library
- **Zod**: Schema validation
- **@hookform/resolvers**: Zod integration

## Form Setup Pattern
```typescript
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import { z } from 'zod';

const formSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(1, 'Name is required'),
  email: z.string().email('Invalid email'),
});

type FormData = z.infer<typeof formSchema>;

const MyForm = () => {
  const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors } } = useForm<FormData>({
    resolver: zodResolver(formSchema),
  });

  const onSubmit = async (data: FormData) => {
    // Handle submission
  };

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
      {/* Form fields */}
    </form>
  );
};
```

## Validation Schemas
- Define schemas in [src/lib/validation-schemas.ts](mdc:src/lib/validation-schemas.ts)
- Use Zod for type-safe validation
- Provide clear error messages
- Support both English and Hindi labels when needed

## Form Field Patterns
- Use consistent field styling
- Display validation errors inline
- Show required field indicators
- Support disabled states

## Form Submission
- Show loading state during submission
- Disable submit button while submitting
- Handle success and error states
- Reset form on successful submission

## Dynamic Forms
- Use [src/components/forms/DynamicForm.tsx](mdc:src/components/forms/DynamicForm.tsx) for dynamic forms
- Support conditional fields
- Handle nested form structures
- Validate dynamically

## Multi-Step Forms
- Use [src/components/forms/MultiStepForm.tsx](mdc:src/components/forms/MultiStepForm.tsx)
- Track current step
- Validate per step
- Save progress between steps

## Form State Management
- Use React Hook Form for form state
- Use local state for UI state (loading, errors)
- Use Redux for global form data when needed
- Persist form data when appropriate

## Common Form Components
- Input fields with validation
- Select dropdowns
- Date pickers
- File uploads
- Checkboxes and radio buttons

## Error Display
```typescript
{errors.fieldName && (
  <p className="text-sm text-red-600 dark:text-red-400 mt-1">
    {errors.fieldName.message}
  </p>
)}
```

## Form Accessibility
- Use proper labels
- Associate errors with fields
- Support keyboard navigation
- Include ARIA attributes
